**Here’s Number 1 – Final Integration Patch**

This is the exact code you need to make the new `EffectSystem` work with your upgraded weapon system.

---

### 1. Import the EffectSystem

At the top of `src/game/engine.ts`:

```ts
import { EffectSystem } from "./effects";
```

---

### 2. Create the EffectSystem

Inside your `start()` method (or wherever you initialize systems), add:

```ts
this.effects = new EffectSystem(this.scene, this.camera);
```

Also declare it in the class:

```ts
private effects!: EffectSystem;
```

---

### 3. Update every frame

Inside your main visual/update loop (usually `visual(dt)` or `frame()`), add:

```ts
this.effects.update(dt);
```

---

### 4. Integration inside `equip()` (Weapon Switch)

Replace your current `equip` method with this fully upgraded version:

```ts
equip(index: number) {
  if (!this.canEquip(index) || index === this.weapon) return;

  // Feedback
  this.audio.ui("equip");
  this.trauma = Math.min(1, this.trauma + 0.28);
  this.vmKickZ = -0.22;
  this.vmKickY = -0.06;
  this.switchLock = 0.18;

  // Crimson flash
  this.effects.muzzleFlash(0xff0033, 14, 0.14);

  // Actual switch
  this.weapon = index;
  this.recoilSim.reset();
  this.charge = 0;
  this.reloadT = 0;
  this.showView(WEAPONS[index].view);
}
```

---

### 5. Integration inside `shoot()`

At the top of your `shoot()` method, keep the lock check, then after you successfully fire, add the effect calls:

```ts
shoot() {
  if (this.switchLock > 0) return;
  if (this.reloadT > 0) return;

  const w = WEAPONS[this.weapon];
  const now = performance.now() / 1000;

  if (now - this.lastShot[this.weapon] < w.cooldown) return;

  if (this.mag[this.weapon] <= 0 && !this.infAmmo) {
    this.audio.ui("empty");
    this.startReload();
    return;
  }

  // Consume ammo
  if (!this.infAmmo) this.mag[this.weapon]--;
  this.lastShot[this.weapon] = now;

  // ===== NEW EFFECTS =====
  const flashColor = (w.fire === "beam" || w.fire === "rail") ? 0xff0033 : 0xff4400;
  this.effects.muzzleFlash(flashColor, w.fire === "melee" ? 9 : 22, 0.07);

  this.recoilSim.fire(w, { ads: this.ads, firstShot: true });
  this.trauma = Math.min(1, this.trauma + (w.fire === "melee" ? 0.18 : 0.32));

  // ===== YOUR ORIGINAL FIRE LOGIC =====
  if (w.fire === "hitscan" || w.fire === "rail") {
    this.hitscan(w.damage, w.spread * this.recoilSim.spreadMul(), w.range);
  } else if (w.fire === "projectile") {
    this.spawnProj(...);
  } else if (w.fire === "melee") {
    this.melee(w.damage, w.range);
  }

  this.audio.weapon(w.nameKey || "shot");
}
```

---

### 6. Optional: Better hit sparks

Wherever you currently call your old spark function after a hit, replace it with:

```ts
this.effects.spark(hitPoint, "energy", 12);   // or "blood", "metal", "rune"
```

---

That’s it.  

After you paste these changes, your weapon switching and gunfire will have the strong crimson flashes, better impact effects, and much higher quality feel.

